* Access-time bench: clock edge to valid Q, and write completion (circuit body for `klt sim`;
* no .control/.end). GENERATED by `array_post.py gen-access` from the top-level instances of
* design/macro/macro.spice; run_array.sh fails if this file is stale.
*
* Representative macro: the real address latch, control, row decoder, data latch and out latch
* (full 32-bit banks), and the real bit slice 0 (2 bit-line pairs x 128 cells, precharge, mux,
* sense amp, write driver) at the selected address. The other 31 I/O are represented by their
* load only: 31 dummy slices (2 precharge, mux, sense amp, write driver on private bit lines)
* on PRE_B / SEL* / SAE / WE / DL[k] / DOUT[k], and 62 bitcells (their access gates) on the selected
* wordline WL[45]. Wordlines of other rows are not loaded: they do not switch at this address.
* Schematic level: no wire parasitics.
*
* Address 0x5A: A[7:1] = 45 selects WL[45], A[0] = 0 selects column 0 (SEL0 high).
* Six cycles, 8 ns period, CLK high 3 ns (rising 50 % at 4.05, 12.05, 20.05, 28.05, 36.05, 44.05 ns):
*   write 1, read (expects 1), write 0, read (expects 0), write 1, read (expects 1).
* The first read only puts a 1 into the output latch; the last read follows a read of 0, so its Q rise is
* a clean transition. CEN low, GWEN = WEN low in the write cycles; address, data and controls change in the
* CLK-low phase (latches transparent), 3 ns before each edge. Every cell starts holding 0 (.ic).
* All levels scale with VDD (request supply corner).
.include ../../design/macro/macro.spice

Vdd vdd 0 DC 1.2
* the macro's VSS port is a net named VSS, not node 0
Vvss VSS 0 DC 0
* thresholds that follow the supply corner
Bthr9 thr9 0 V = 0.9*v(vdd)
Bthr5 thr5 0 V = 0.5*v(vdd)
Bthr1 thr1 0 V = 0.1*v(vdd)
* clock: unit pulse x VDD
Vpclk pclk 0 PULSE(0 1 4n 100p 100p 3n 8n)
Bclk CLK 0 V = v(pclk)*v(vdd)
Bclkm clkm 0 V = v(CLK)
Bcen CEN 0 V = 0
* GWEN = WEN: low (write) in cycles 1 and 3, high (read) in cycles 2 and 4
Vpgw pgw 0 PWL(0 0 9n 0 9.1n 1 17n 1 17.1n 0 25n 0 25.1n 1 33n 1 33.1n 0 41n 0 41.1n 1 57n 1)
Bgwen GWEN 0 V = v(pgw)*v(vdd)
Bwen  WEN  0 V = v(pgw)*v(vdd)
* D[0]: 1 for the first write, 0 for the second
Vpd0 pd0 0 PWL(0 1 17n 1 17.1n 0 25n 0 25.1n 1 57n 1)
Bd0 D[0] 0 V = v(pd0)*v(vdd)
